/P 110 0 R
/E (This project details the development of Sensoria, an autonomous robot engineered for the WRO Future Engineers challenge. Our team combined skills in C++ programming, 3D CAD modeling, and circuit design to create a custom vehicle capable of completing multi-lap track navigation and obstacle avoidance. Designed around strict size limits, low center-of-gravity requirements, and real-time vision processing constraints, Sensoria autonomously detects color-coded traffic blocks and uses sensor feedback to make split-second steering corrections while maintaining high-speed lap stability.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [0]
>>
